{
  "id": "contrast-grid",
  "title": "WCAG Contrast Grid",
  "summary": "Every foreground/background pair in a palette, scored against WCAG 2.1 contrast thresholds and labelled AAA / AA / AA-Large / fail.",
  "description": "A palette is only usable in the combinations that actually pass contrast, and that is not obvious by eye — mid-tone accents on dark surfaces fail far more often than designers expect. This specimen takes a set of tokens, computes the real WCAG 2.1 contrast ratio for every foreground-on-background pair, and renders the matrix with each cell showing its ratio and grade. The maths is the spec formula, not an approximation: sRGB channels are linearised, relative luminance is weighted 0.2126/0.7152/0.0722, and the ratio is (L_light + 0.05) / (L_dark + 0.05).",
