  "dependencies": [],
  "browser_support": "All modern browsers. Plain DOM and arithmetic, no color-space APIs required.",
  "performance_notes": "One pass over N×N pairs at load; a 6-token palette is 36 cells. Nothing animates and nothing recomputes unless the palette changes.",
  "accessibility_notes": "The grid is a real table with scope-ed headers, so it reads correctly in a screen reader. Grade is never carried by colour alone — every cell states its ratio and its grade as text. Note WCAG 2.1 ratios ignore how the eye actually responds at low luminance; APCA (WCAG 3 draft) scores dark-mode pairs more faithfully, so treat a bare pass on dark surfaces as a floor, not a target.",
  "customization": [
