  "ai_usage": "Use this to audit a palette BEFORE committing tokens, and to answer 'can I put this colour on that one'. Drop your tokens into PALETTE as {name, hex} and read the matrix.\n\nThe formula, if you are reimplementing it: convert each sRGB channel to 0–1, linearise with c <= 0.03928 ? c/12.92 : ((c+0.055)/1.055)^2.4, take L = 0.2126R + 0.7152G + 0.0722B, then ratio = (Llighter + 0.05) / (Ldarker + 0.05). Ratio runs 1 (identical) to 21 (black on white). Thresholds: 4.5 for body text (AA), 7 for AAA, 3 for large text (18pt / 14pt bold) and for non-text UI such as icons, focus rings, and input borders.\n\nApply it: body copy needs 4.5 minimum — do not ship a 3.2 accent as a text colour just because it looks fine to you on a calibrated display. Placeholder text, disabled states, and thin icon strokes are the usual silent failures. Contrast is symmetric, so the matrix is mirrored; you only need one triangle.\n\nCaveats worth passing on: WCAG 2.1 is known to be lenient on dark backgrounds and harsh on mid-tones, so a 4.6 on a near-black surface can still read poorly — prefer APCA there. And never encode pass/fail in colour alone in your own UI; state the number.",
  "path": "effects/color-systems/contrast-grid.html",
  "source": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>WCAG Contrast Grid</title>\n  <script type=\"application/json\" id=\"effect-meta\">\n  {\n    \"id\": \"contrast-grid\",\n    \"title\": \"WCAG Contrast Grid\",\n    \"summary\": \"Every foreground/background pair in a palette, scored against WCAG 2.1 contrast thresholds and labelled AAA / AA / AA-Large / fail.\",\n    \"description\": \"A palette is only usable in the combinations that actually pass contrast, and that is not obvious by eye — mid-tone accents on dark surfaces fail far more often than designers expect. This specimen takes a set of tokens, computes the real WCAG 2.1 contrast ratio for every foreground-on-background pair, and renders the matrix with each cell showing its ratio and grade. The maths is the spec formula, not an approximation: sRGB channels are linearised, relative luminance is weighted 0.2126/0.7152/0.0722, and the ratio is (L_light + 0.05) / (L_dark + 0.05).\",\n    \"theme\": \"color-systems\",\n    \"categories\": [\"color\", \"accessibility\", \"design-tokens\", \"reference\"],\n    \"tags\": [\"contrast\", \"wcag\", \"accessibility\", \"a11y\", \"color\", \"palette\", \"tokens\", \"luminance\", \"ratio\", \"audit\"],\n    \"tech\": [\"css\", \"js\"],\n    \"era\": \"timeless\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"intermediate\",\n    \"dependencies\": [],\n    \"browser_support\": \"All modern browsers. Plain DOM and arithmetic, no color-space APIs required.\",\n    \"performance_notes\": \"One pass over N×N pairs at load; a 6-token palette is 36 cells. Nothing animates and nothing recomputes unless the palette changes.\",\n    \"accessibility_notes\": \"The grid is a real table with scope-ed headers, so it reads correctly in a screen reader. Grade is never carried by colour alone — every cell states its ratio and its grade as text. Note WCAG 2.1 ratios ignore how the eye actually responds at low luminance; APCA (WCAG 3 draft) scores dark-mode pairs more faithfully, so treat a bare pass on dark surfaces as a floor, not a target.\",\n    \"customization\": [\n      { \"name\": \"PALETTE\", \"description\": \"The tokens to cross-check — swap in your own name/hex pairs\", \"default\": \"6 tokens\" },\n      { \"name\": \"thresholds\", \"description\": \"WCAG 2.1 cutoffs: 7 = AAA, 4.5 = AA, 3 = AA Large (18pt+/14pt bold) and non-text UI\", \"default\": \"7 / 4.5 / 3\" }\n    ],\n    \"variations\": [\n      \"Restrict rows to text tokens and columns to surface tokens — the pairs you would actually ship\",\n      \"Emit the failures as a build-time check that fails CI when a shipped pair regresses\",\n      \"Score with APCA instead for dark-heavy interfaces\",\n      \"Add a column for the smallest passing font size per pair\"\n    ],\n    \"related\": [\"semantic-color-tokens\", \"dark-mode-tokens\", \"oklch-gradient\"],\n    \"ai_usage\": \"Use this to audit a palette BEFORE committing tokens, and to answer 'can I put this colour on that one'. Drop your tokens into PALETTE as {name, hex} and read the matrix.\\n\\nThe formula, if you are reimplementing it: convert each sRGB channel to 0–1, linearise with c <= 0.03928 ? c/12.92 : ((c+0.055)/1.055)^2.4, take L = 0.2126R + 0.7152G + 0.0722B, then ratio = (Llighter + 0.05) / (Ldarker + 0.05). Ratio runs 1 (identical) to 21 (black on white). Thresholds: 4.5 for body text (AA), 7 for AAA, 3 for large text (18pt / 14pt bold) and for non-text UI such as icons, focus rings, and input borders.\\n\\nApply it: body copy needs 4.5 minimum — do not ship a 3.2 accent as a text colour just because it looks fine to you on a calibrated display. Placeholder text, disabled states, and thin icon strokes are the usual silent failures. Contrast is symmetric, so the matrix is mirrored; you only need one triangle.\\n\\nCaveats worth passing on: WCAG 2.1 is known to be lenient on dark backgrounds and harsh on mid-tones, so a 4.6 on a near-black surface can still read poorly — prefer APCA there. And never encode pass/fail in colour alone in your own UI; state the number.\"\n  }\n  </script>\n  <style>\n    :root {\n      --bg: #0b0d12;\n      --surface: #12151f;\n      --line: #262c3d;\n      --text: #e7ebf3;\n      --muted: #8b93a7;\n      --pass: #2dd4bf;\n      --warn: #f5b445;\n      --fail: #f2555a;\n    }\n    * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n    html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; }\n    body {\n      background: var(--bg); color: var(--text);\n      font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; padding: 1rem;\n      display: grid; align-content: center; justify-items: center;\n    }\n    table { border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .62rem; }\n    caption {\n      caption-side: top; text-align: left; padding-bottom: .6rem;\n      font-size: .7rem; color: var(--muted); letter-spacing: .04em;\n    }\n    caption b { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0; }\n    th, td { border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: .3rem .34rem; text-align: center; }\n    thead th, tbody th { background: var(--surface); color: var(--muted); font-weight: 500; }\n    tbody th { text-align: right; }\n    .sw {\n      display: inline-block; width: 9px; height: 9px; border-radius: 2px;\n      margin-right: .28rem; vertical-align: -1px; border: 1px solid #ffffff22;\n    }\n    td { font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; line-height: 1.25; }\n    td .r { display: block; font-size: .68rem; font-weight: 600; }\n    td .g { display: block; font-size: .52rem; letter-spacing: .06em; opacity: .85; }\n    /* The ratio is drawn in the actual fg-on-bg pair, so a failing pair looks\n       as bad as it scores. The grade beneath it carries an auto-picked ink so\n       the reading is never itself a contrast failure. */\n    td .g { border-radius: 3px; padding: 0 .2rem; font-weight: 700; }\n    .self { color: #4a5268; }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <table id=\"grid\">\n    <caption><b>WCAG 2.1 contrast</b> — foreground (row) on background (column)</caption>\n  </table>\n\n  <script>\n    // Swap these for your own tokens; everything below is derived.\n    var PALETTE = [\n      { name: \"text\",    hex: \"#e7ebf3\" },\n      { name: \"muted\",   hex: \"#8b93a7\" },\n      { name: \"accent\",  hex: \"#7c5cff\" },\n      { name: \"accent-2\",hex: \"#2dd4bf\" },\n      { name: \"surface\", hex: \"#12151f\" },\n      { name: \"bg\",      hex: \"#0b0d12\" }\n    ];\n\n    // WCAG 2.1 relative luminance: linearise each sRGB channel, then weight it.\n    function luminance(hex) {\n      var n = parseInt(hex.slice(1), 16);\n      var ch = [(n >> 16) & 255, (n >> 8) & 255, n & 255].map(function (v) {\n        var c = v / 255;\n        return c <= 0.03928 ? c / 12.92 : Math.pow((c + 0.055) / 1.055, 2.4);\n      });\n      return 0.2126 * ch[0] + 0.7152 * ch[1] + 0.0722 * ch[2];\n    }\n    function ratio(a, b) {\n      var la = luminance(a), lb = luminance(b);\n      var hi = Math.max(la, lb), lo = Math.min(la, lb);\n      return (hi + 0.05) / (lo + 0.05);\n    }\n    // WCAG 2.1 cutoffs. 3 also covers non-text UI (icons, focus rings, borders).\n    function grade(r) {\n      if (r >= 7) return { cls: \"aaa\", label: \"AAA\" };\n      if (r >= 4.5) return { cls: \"aa\", label: \"AA\" };\n      if (r >= 3) return { cls: \"aal\", label: \"AA LG\" };\n      return { cls: \"no\", label: \"FAIL\" };\n    }\n\n    // Black or white ink, whichever scores higher against this background.\n    function pickInk(hex) {\n      var onWhite = ratio(hex, \"#ffffff\"), onBlack = ratio(hex, \"#000000\");\n      return onBlack >= onWhite\n        ? { fg: \"#000000\", bg: \"#ffffffcc\" }\n        : { fg: \"#ffffff\", bg: \"#00000099\" };\n    }\n\n    var table = document.getElementById(\"grid\");\n    var head = document.createElement(\"thead\");\n    var hr = document.createElement(\"tr\");\n    hr.appendChild(document.createElement(\"td\"));\n    PALETTE.forEach(function (c) {\n      var th = document.createElement(\"th\");\n      th.scope = \"col\";\n      th.innerHTML = '<span class=\"sw\" style=\"background:' + c.hex + '\"></span>' + c.name;\n      hr.appendChild(th);\n    });\n    head.appendChild(hr);\n    table.appendChild(head);\n\n    var body = document.createElement(\"tbody\");\n    PALETTE.forEach(function (fg) {\n      var tr = document.createElement(\"tr\");\n      var th = document.createElement(\"th\");\n      th.scope = \"row\";\n      th.innerHTML = '<span class=\"sw\" style=\"background:' + fg.hex + '\"></span>' + fg.name;\n      tr.appendChild(th);\n      PALETTE.forEach(function (bg) {\n        var td = document.createElement(\"td\");\n        if (fg.hex === bg.hex) {\n          td.className = \"self\";\n          td.innerHTML = '<span class=\"r\">—</span><span class=\"g\">SAME</span>';\n        } else {\n          var r = ratio(fg.hex, bg.hex), g = grade(r);\n          td.style.background = bg.hex;\n          td.style.color = fg.hex;\n          var ink = pickInk(bg.hex);\n          // Grade is stated as text, never carried by colour alone.\n          td.innerHTML =\n            '<span class=\"r\">' + r.toFixed(2) + '</span>' +\n            '<span class=\"g\" style=\"color:' + ink.fg + ';background:' + ink.bg + '\">' + g.label + '</span>';\n        }\n        tr.appendChild(td);\n      });\n      body.appendChild(tr);\n    });\n    table.appendChild(body);\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
}
